# Fulkrum environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and add only what you need:
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env.local     (PowerShell)
#   cp .env.example .env.local            (bash)
#
# Every value here is read by the local API bridge only. API keys are never
# bundled into the browser build and are never returned by the status endpoint.
# Restart `npm run dev` after changing this file.

# --- Provider API keys -------------------------------------------------------
# Each role routes to a provider; a provider without a key refuses its calls
# with a 409 naming the fix, unless its auth style is "none" (set per provider
# in the settings drawer).
# A key entered in the settings drawer is stored in the local database and used
# in place of these; an environment variable here takes precedence over a stored
# key of the same provider.
XAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
GLM_API_KEY=
ZAI_API_KEY=
KIMI_API_KEY=
MOONSHOT_API_KEY=

# --- Model overrides ---------------------------------------------------------
# A route that names an explicit model wins; these set each provider's default
# model for routes that do not.
FULKRUM_GROK_MODEL=grok-4
FULKRUM_OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5
FULKRUM_ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-4-1
FULKRUM_GOOGLE_MODEL=gemini-2.5-pro
FULKRUM_DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-chat
FULKRUM_GLM_MODEL=glm-4.5
FULKRUM_KIMI_MODEL=kimi-k2

# --- Provider endpoints ------------------------------------------------------
# Point a built-in provider at a gateway or a proxy. A custom provider added in
# the settings drawer carries its own base URL instead.
# XAI_BASE_URL=https://api.x.ai/v1
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1
# GOOGLE_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta
# DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1
# GLM_BASE_URL=https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/paas/v4
# KIMI_BASE_URL=https://api.moonshot.ai/v1

# Sampling: a temperature is sent only where the model accepts one. Models known
# to reject a custom temperature (gpt-5, the o series, deepseek-reasoner) omit it,
# and a provider that answers 400 complaining about temperature is retried without
# it and remembered. Override per provider in the settings drawer.
# FULKRUM_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=4096

# Ordered fallback routes, tried when the primary provider fails after retries.
# Comma-separated "Provider label · model" values.
# FULKRUM_FALLBACK_ROUTES=OpenAI · gpt-5,Google · gemini-2.5-pro

# --- Local API bridge --------------------------------------------------------
# The bridge binds 127.0.0.1 only. It is never exposed to the network.
FULKRUM_API_PORT=8787

# Serve the built UI from the bridge itself, so one process is enough:
#   npm run build && npm start
# `npm start` turns this on when a build is present; `npm run dev` does not need it.
# FULKRUM_SERVE_UI=1
# FULKRUM_DIST_DIR=dist

# Workspace root the agent tools may touch. Defaults to the process working
# directory. Paths outside it are refused.
# FULKRUM_WORKSPACE_ROOT=D:\projects\fulkrum

# --- Persistence -------------------------------------------------------------
# A database file, or a directory containing fulkrum.sqlite.
# FULKRUM_DB_PATH=./data/fulkrum.sqlite
# FULKRUM_DATA_DIR=./data

# --- Skills, plugins, blueprints, marketplace ----------------------------------
# Folders of markdown knowledge packs, declarative HTTP tool manifests, and team
# blueprints. Each defaults to a folder of that name under the workspace root;
# "off" disables that kind entirely.
# FULKRUM_SKILLS_DIR=./skills
# FULKRUM_PLUGINS_DIR=./plugins
# FULKRUM_BLUEPRINTS_DIR=./team-blueprints

# Signed skills/plugins index to browse. Empty disables the marketplace; only
# content signed by the pinned key is ever believed.
# FULKRUM_MARKETPLACE_URL=https://example.com/fulkrum-index.json
# FULKRUM_MARKETPLACE_KEY=

# --- Security policy ---------------------------------------------------------
# Browser origins allowed to call the API. Non-browser clients (curl, scripts)
# send no Origin header and are always allowed; a browser page on any other
# origin is refused with 403. Vite's preview server uses port 4173, so add it
# here if you run `npm run preview`.
FULKRUM_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://127.0.0.1:5173,http://localhost:5173

# Host allowlist for the http.request tool. Default deny: with this unset the
# tool requires explicit approval every time. Comma-separated hostnames;
# subdomains of a listed host are allowed.
# FULKRUM_HTTP_ALLOWLIST=api.example.com,docs.example.com

# Custom provider URLs must use a public host, because loopback and private
# network targets are blocked to stop the agent from reaching services on your
# own machine. Set this to 1 to allow a local model gateway such as Ollama.
# FULKRUM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_PROVIDER_URLS=1

# --- Budgets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Hard ceilings in US dollars. A run stops in a budget_exceeded state instead of
# silently spending more, and the control room offers to raise the ceiling and
# continue. Unset means no ceiling. A budget only works for models whose price is
# known: unpriced calls are reported as "cost unknown" rather than counted as
# free, and the run says so.
# FULKRUM_RUN_BUDGET_USD=2.00
# FULKRUM_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=10.00

# The daily ceiling resets at local midnight; set this to UTC for a window that
# does not move with daylight saving.
# FULKRUM_BUDGET_TIMEZONE=

# What a call in flight is assumed to cost against a ceiling. Cost is only known
# after a call returns, so without a reservation every parallel reader passes the
# same check; the estimate is the largest call this run has already made, or this
# floor.
# FULKRUM_BUDGET_RESERVE_USD=0.02

# Where prices live. The built-in table is approximate published list pricing and
# is meant to be corrected for the models you use: point this at a JSON file of
# the same shape (model -> {input, output, cacheRead, cacheWrite} in USD per
# million tokens) to override entries without editing code.
# FULKRUM_PRICE_FILE=./prices.json

# --- Agent loop --------------------------------------------------------------
# How many tool calls a worker may make on one task before it must summarise.
# FULKRUM_MAX_TOOL_STEPS=8

# Files longer than this are not diffed in the artifacts view; the change is
# reported as too large to diff rather than dumped in full.
# FULKRUM_MAX_DIFF_LINES=2000

# How much of a file's previous contents are kept so its change can be reviewed.
# Larger files keep their size and hash but not their bytes.
# FULKRUM_MAX_SNAPSHOT_BYTES=64000

# Read-only research tasks may run this many at a time. Tasks that can write are
# always serialized, because parallel writers conflict over the same files.
# FULKRUM_MAX_PARALLEL_RESEARCHERS=3

# Upper bound on a single model reply.
# FULKRUM_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=4096

# Handoffs carry a bounded digest — summary plus evidence and artifact pointers —
# instead of whole transcripts. Evidence records per completion are capped too.
# FULKRUM_HANDOFF_MAX_CHARS=4000
# FULKRUM_EVIDENCE_MAX_ITEMS=20

# Verifiers and reviewers get a few read-only steps, and a task may be attempted
# this many times including repairs before the run stops or replans.
# FULKRUM_VERIFY_MAX_STEPS=3
# FULKRUM_TASK_MAX_ATTEMPTS=2

# Approximate tokens a task may hold in context before old tool results compact
# into cited stubs, and how many workspace files a shell receipt may name
# (0 disables the before/after manifest).
# FULKRUM_TASK_TOKEN_BUDGET=200000
# FULKRUM_SHELL_MANIFEST_MAX_FILES=2000

# Finished run traces go here as OTLP/HTTP JSON when set; empty disables export.
# FULKRUM_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:4318/v1/traces

# Per-request provider timeout, and how many attempts a retryable failure gets.
# FULKRUM_PROVIDER_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
# FULKRUM_PROVIDER_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3

# How many calls may be in flight to one provider before the extras queue, and
# when a provider that keeps failing is skipped. Only failures worth retrying
# count: a 400 means the request was wrong, not that the provider is down. After
# the cooldown one call is let through as a probe.
# FULKRUM_PROVIDER_MAX_CONCURRENCY=3
# FULKRUM_BREAKER_THRESHOLD=3
# FULKRUM_BREAKER_COOLDOWN_MS=30000

# Outbound HTTP from the http.request tool: how much of a response body is read
# before the connection is cut, and how long a single request may take. The body
# is streamed and abandoned at the cap rather than buffered whole.
# FULKRUM_MAX_HTTP_BODY_BYTES=1000000
# FULKRUM_HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# A provider response larger than this is treated as an error rather than parsed.
# FULKRUM_MAX_PROVIDER_BYTES=8000000

# --- Execution boundary ------------------------------------------------------
# Agent commands run inside a container, never on the host. When no engine is
# reachable, command execution is disabled and the app says so; it never falls
# back to running on Windows.
#
# WSL2 is where the engine runs, not what contains it: a WSL distribution can
# execute Windows binaries through its interop layer, so "inside WSL" is not a
# boundary.
#
# Build the runner image once (from server/runner):
#   npm run runner:build        (or: docker build -t fulkrum-runner:local server/runner)
#
# Leave empty to auto-detect: the Docker or Podman CLI on PATH, then Docker
# inside the default WSL distribution. Set it explicitly to skip detection:
#   docker       Docker CLI on PATH (Docker Desktop with the WSL2 backend)
#   docker-wsl   Docker Engine installed inside the default WSL distribution
#   podman       Podman on PATH
# FULKRUM_CONTAINER_ENGINE=

# Container runtime for agent commands. Empty means the engine default; runsc
# runs each command under a gVisor user-space kernel, which interposes syscalls
# between the container and the host for stronger isolation at some syscall cost.
# FULKRUM_CONTAINER_RUNTIME=

# Absolute path to the engine CLI, for shells where it is not on PATH. A service
# or non-interactive shell on Windows often lacks the per-user Docker directory,
# which shows up as `spawn docker ENOENT` even though Docker Desktop is running.
# FULKRUM_CONTAINER_CLI=C:\Users\you\AppData\Local\Programs\DockerDesktop\resources\bin\docker.exe

# Runner image. The image is part of the boundary, so pin the digest after
# building or pulling: a tag can be moved, a digest cannot. The boot log prints
# the digest and the image id it found, and says so when the image is only tagged.
#   docker inspect --format='{{index .RepoDigests 0}}' fulkrum-runner:local
FULKRUM_RUNNER_IMAGE=fulkrum-runner:local

# Per-container limits, and the identity the command runs as. By default the uid
# is the one that owns the workspace, because a bind mount keeps the host's
# ownership and any other uid cannot write to it. Set it to override, or use
# FULKRUM_RUNNER_USERNS=keep-id with rootless Podman to map your host user in.
# FULKRUM_CONTAINER_MEMORY=2g
# FULKRUM_CONTAINER_CPUS=2
# FULKRUM_CONTAINER_PIDS=256
# FULKRUM_EXEC_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
# FULKRUM_RUNNER_USER=
# FULKRUM_RUNNER_USERNS=
# FULKRUM_RUNNER_NOFILE=1024

# --- Retention ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Tool outputs, their raw inputs, and finished tasks' turns are pruned on this
# window. Run events are hash-chained and retained indefinitely: deleting one
# would break the chain. The bytes live on the tool call, and the chain records
# their hash, so pruning shrinks the database without breaking verification.
# FULKRUM_TOOL_OUTPUT_RETENTION_DAYS=14

# --- Durability --------------------------------------------------------------
# The head of each run's hash chain is written to an append-only file next to the
# database as well as to a row inside it. The row alone cannot notice being
# deleted along with the events it vouched for; the file can. Set it to `off` to
# stop writing anchors, or to an absolute path to put them elsewhere.
# FULKRUM_ANCHOR_FILE=./data/audit-heads.log

# A copy is taken at boot when the newest one is older than this many hours, with
# VACUUM INTO, so nothing has to stop. 0 disables it. The newest few are kept.
# FULKRUM_BACKUP_INTERVAL_HOURS=24
# FULKRUM_BACKUP_KEEP=7

# WAL pages are checkpointed back into the main file after this many.
# FULKRUM_WAL_AUTOCHECKPOINT=1000
